  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Washington totaled $497M in FY2027 to date. The federal government reported 3,128 awards, with an average award size of $159K. Obligations fell 97.5% year over year. Yearly context shows a peak in FY26 at $19.5B, then declining through FY27 to $497M. The Department of Energy is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $353M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $57.7M and the Department of Homeland Security at $31M. BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE received the largest single share of obligations at $140M, with HANFORD TANK WASTE OPERATIONS & CLOSURE, LLC and BECHTEL NATIONAL, INC. receiving $117M and $73M respectively. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry at $140M, and Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal follows at $117M. This snapshot reflects a sharp year-over-year reduction in obligations and a FY2027 to date program concentrated in energy, cleanup, and research-related contractors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are driving federal spending in Washington?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is driving spending in Washington, obligating $353M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $57.7M and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $31M. The Department of Agriculture, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of Transportation also appear among the top buyers with $15.9M, $8.7M, and $7.3M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries capture the largest contract shares?",
        "body": "BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE captured the largest vendor share at $140M, with HANFORD TANK WASTE OPERATIONS & CLOSURE, LLC at $117M and BECHTEL NATIONAL, INC. at $73M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry at $140M, and Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal is second at $117M. Security Guards and Patrol Services and Remediation Services also appear in the top industries with $30.1M and $21.3M respectively."
      }
    ]
